' True when the server's `/system/configuration/encoding` response advertises
' fallback-font support.
'
' Every operand is type-checked rather than negated directly. The crash this
' replaces (#582) was `not r.json.EnableFallbackFont` faulting with `&h18` —
' "Operator 'not' can't be applied to 'Invalid'" — against a server that
' answered 200 with a valid encoding config that simply omits the field. A
' missing key dereferences to Invalid, and while `Invalid = true` is merely
' false, `not Invalid` is a type mismatch. The guard crashed instead of
' reaching the fallback it exists to select.
'
' @param response - an `rr_Requests()` response AA
' @return true only when the server explicitly advertises the capability
function serverSupportsFallbackFont(response as dynamic) as boolean
  if LCase(type(response)) <> "roassociativearray" then return false
  if response.ok <> true then return false
  if LCase(type(response.json)) <> "roassociativearray" then return false
  return response.json.EnableFallbackFont = true
end function
